{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Machine Learning Prediction of Steel Yield Strength\n","\n","A materials-engineering workflow for predicting steel yield strength from alloy chemistry and processing/heat-treatment information.\n","\n","**Scope:** chemistry + processing-state features form the core model; validated quench/temper temperature information is then evaluated as an augmented feature set.\n","\n","> **Validation note:** hyperparameter selection was performed before the reported 20% holdout evaluation. The holdout is therefore a comparative evaluation, while the leakage-free 5-fold pipeline is the primary robustness estimate."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 1. Setup and Data Loading"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["from pathlib import Path\n","import re\n","import numpy as np\n","import pandas as pd\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split, KFold, cross_validate\n","from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n","from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n","from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestRegressor\n","from sklearn.metrics import mean_absolute_error, mean_squared_error, r2_score\n","from sklearn.inspection import permutation_importance\n","\n","RANDOM_STATE = 42\n","DATA_PATH = Path('../data/Steel database with labelled clusters.xlsx')\n","\n","df = pd.read_excel(DATA_PATH)\n","print('Original shape:', df.shape)\n","display(df.head())"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 2. Data Cleaning and Deduplication"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# Remove empty/unnamed columns created by the source spreadsheet.\n","empty_cols = [c for c in df.columns if str(c).startswith('Unnamed:')]\n","df = df.drop(columns=empty_cols, errors='ignore').copy()\n","\n","target = 'Yield strength (MPa)'\n","\n","# Investigate duplicates independently of the entry identifier.\n","dedup_cols = [c for c in df.columns if c != 'Entry']\n","duplicate_count = df.duplicated(subset=dedup_cols, keep=False).sum()\n","df_deduplicated = df.drop_duplicates(subset=dedup_cols, keep='first').copy()\n","\n","print('Removed empty columns:', empty_cols)\n","print('Duplicate rows identified (ignoring Entry):', duplicate_count)\n","print('Deduplicated shape:', df_deduplicated.shape)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 3. Processing-State Feature Engineering"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["df_features = df_deduplicated.copy()\n","processing_lower = df_features['Processing condition'].fillna('').astype(str).str.lower()\n","\n","processing_flags = {\n","    'is_quenched': 'quenched',\n","    'is_tempered': 'temper',\n","    'is_annealed': 'anneal',\n","    'is_aged': 'aged',\n","    'is_carburized': 'carbur',\n","    'is_normalized': 'normaliz',\n","    'is_cold_drawn': 'cold drawn',\n","    'is_hot_rolled': 'hot rolled',\n","    'is_as_rolled': 'as rolled',\n","    'is_air_cooled': 'air cooled',\n","}\n","\n","for feature, keyword in processing_flags.items():\n","    df_features[feature] = processing_lower.str.contains(keyword, regex=False).astype(int)\n","\n","display(df_features[['Processing condition'] + list(processing_flags)].head(10))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 4. Validated Temperature Extraction"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["processing = df_features['Processing condition'].fillna('').astype(str)\n","\n","# High-confidence quench patterns used in the analysis.\n","water_quench_temp = processing.str.extract(\n","    r'water\\s+quenched\\s+(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)\\s*°?\\s*C', expand=False, flags=re.I\n",")\n","reheated_oil_quench_temp = processing.str.extract(\n","    r'reheated\\s+to\\s+(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)\\s*°?\\s*C.*?oil\\s+quenched', expand=False, flags=re.I\n",")\n","oil_quench_temp = processing.str.extract(\n","    r'oil\\s+quenched.{0,100}?\\((\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)\\s*°?\\s*C', expand=False, flags=re.I\n",")\n","quench_temp_final = water_quench_temp.combine_first(reheated_oil_quench_temp).combine_first(oil_quench_temp)\n","\n","# Tempering temperature: capture a temperature associated with 'tempered'.\n","temper_temp_v2 = processing.str.extract(\n","    r'\\btempered\\b(?:(?!carburized)[^0-9]){0,25}(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)\\s*°?\\s*C',\n","    expand=False, flags=re.I\n",")\n","\n","df_features['quench_temp_C'] = pd.to_numeric(quench_temp_final, errors='coerce')\n","df_features['temper_temp_C'] = pd.to_numeric(temper_temp_v2, errors='coerce')\n","\n","print('Quench temperatures extracted:', df_features['quench_temp_C'].notna().sum())\n","print('Temper temperatures extracted:', df_features['temper_temp_C'].notna().sum())\n","display(df_features[['Processing condition','quench_temp_C','temper_temp_C']].head(15))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 5. Modeling Feature Sets"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["composition_features = [\n","    'Al','Cu','Mn','N','Ni','Ti','S','Fe','Zr','P','Si','V','Mo','Co','C','Nb','B','Cr'\n","]\n","processing_features = list(processing_flags)\n","core_features = composition_features + processing_features\n","\n","model_df = df_features[core_features + [target]].copy()\n","model_df = model_df.dropna(subset=[target]).copy()\n","X = model_df[core_features].copy()\n","y = model_df[target].copy()\n","\n","print('Modeling dataset:', model_df.shape)\n","print('Core feature count:', len(core_features))\n","print('Target missing values:', y.isna().sum())\n","print('Unique records used:', len(model_df))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 6. Train/Test Split"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n","    X, y, test_size=0.20, random_state=RANDOM_STATE\n",")\n","print('Training samples:', len(X_train))\n","print('Test samples:', len(X_test))\n","print('Training target mean:', y_train.mean())\n","print('Test target mean:', y_test.mean())"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 7. Tuned Core Random Forest"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["# Best hyperparameters selected during the completed analysis.\n","best_params = {\n","    'n_estimators': 495,\n","    'max_depth': 30,\n","    'max_features': 0.75,\n","    'min_samples_leaf': 1,\n","    'min_samples_split': 7,\n","}\n","\n","core_model = RandomForestRegressor(\n","    **best_params, random_state=RANDOM_STATE, n_jobs=-1\n",")\n","core_model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n","core_pred = core_model.predict(X_test)\n","\n","core_mae = mean_absolute_error(y_test, core_pred)\n","core_rmse = np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(y_test, core_pred))\n","core_r2 = r2_score(y_test, core_pred)\n","\n","print(f'Core MAE : {core_mae:.2f} MPa')\n","print(f'Core RMSE: {core_rmse:.2f} MPa')\n","print(f'Core R²  : {core_r2:.4f}')"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 8. Temperature-Augmented Features"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["X_aug_raw = df_features.loc[model_df.index, core_features].copy()\n","\n","for col in ['quench_temp_C', 'temper_temp_C']:\n","    X_aug_raw[col] = pd.to_numeric(df_features.loc[model_df.index, col], errors='coerce')\n","    X_aug_raw[f'{col}_missing'] = X_aug_raw[col].isna().astype(int)\n","\n","print('Augmented feature count:', X_aug_raw.shape[1])\n","display(X_aug_raw[['quench_temp_C','temper_temp_C','quench_temp_C_missing','temper_temp_C_missing']].describe())"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 9. Leakage-Free 5-Fold Cross-Validation"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["cv = KFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=RANDOM_STATE)\n","\n","final_aug_pipeline = Pipeline([\n","    ('imputer', SimpleImputer(strategy='median')),\n","    ('random_forest', RandomForestRegressor(\n","        **best_params, random_state=RANDOM_STATE, n_jobs=-1\n","    ))\n,"]])\n","\n","cv_out = cross_validate(\n","    final_aug_pipeline, X_aug_raw, y, cv=cv,\n","    scoring={'MAE':'neg_mean_absolute_error','RMSE':'neg_root_mean_squared_error','R2':'r2'},\n","    n_jobs=-1\n",")\n","\n","cv_summary = pd.DataFrame({\n","    'Fold': range(1,6),\n","    'MAE (MPa)': -cv_out['test_MAE'],\n","    'RMSE (MPa)': -cv_out['test_RMSE'],\n","    'R²': cv_out['test_R2']\n","})\n","display(cv_summary.round(4))\n","print(f'Mean MAE : {-cv_out[\"test_MAE\"].mean():.2f} ± {cv_out[\"test_MAE\"].std():.2f} MPa')\n","print(f'Mean RMSE: {-cv_out[\"test_RMSE\"].mean():.2f} ± {cv_out[\"test_RMSE\"].std():.2f} MPa')\n","print(f'Mean R²  : {cv_out[\"test_R2\"].mean():.4f} ± {cv_out[\"test_R2\"].std():.4f}')"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 10. Final Temperature-Augmented Holdout Evaluation"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["X_train_aug, X_test_aug, y_train_aug, y_test_aug = train_test_split(\n","    X_aug_raw, y, test_size=0.20, random_state=RANDOM_STATE\n",")\n","\n","final_aug_pipeline.fit(X_train_aug, y_train_aug)\n","aug_pred = final_aug_pipeline.predict(X_test_aug)\n","\n","aug_mae = mean_absolute_error(y_test_aug, aug_pred)\n","aug_rmse = np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(y_test_aug, aug_pred))\n","aug_r2 = r2_score(y_test_aug, aug_pred)\n","\n","print(f'Temperature-augmented MAE : {aug_mae:.2f} MPa')\n","print(f'Temperature-augmented RMSE: {aug_rmse:.2f} MPa')\n","print(f'Temperature-augmented R²  : {aug_r2:.4f}')"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 11. Core vs Temperature-Augmented Model"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["comparison = pd.DataFrame({\n","    'Model': ['Core Random Forest','Temperature-Augmented Random Forest'],\n","    'MAE (MPa)': [core_mae, aug_mae],\n","    'RMSE (MPa)': [core_rmse, aug_rmse],\n","    'R²': [core_r2, aug_r2]\n","})\n","display(comparison.round(4))\n","\n","print(f'MAE improvement: {core_mae-aug_mae:.2f} MPa ({(core_mae-aug_mae)/core_mae*100:.2f}%)')\n","print(f'RMSE improvement: {core_rmse-aug_rmse:.2f} MPa ({(core_rmse-aug_rmse)/core_rmse*100:.2f}%)')\n","print(f'R² improvement: {aug_r2-core_r2:.4f} ({(aug_r2-core_r2)/core_r2*100:.2f}%)')"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 12. Actual vs Predicted"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["plt.figure(figsize=(8,7))\n","plt.scatter(y_test_aug, aug_pred, alpha=0.65)\n","lo = min(y_test_aug.min(), aug_pred.min())\n","hi = max(y_test_aug.max(), aug_pred.max())\n","plt.plot([lo,hi],[lo,hi], linestyle='--')\n","plt.xlabel('Actual Yield Strength (MPa)')\n","plt.ylabel('Predicted Yield Strength (MPa)')\n","plt.title('Temperature-Augmented Random Forest: Actual vs Predicted')\n","plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 13. Residual Analysis"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["errors = aug_pred - y_test_aug.values\n","residuals = pd.DataFrame({\n","    'Actual Yield Strength (MPa)': y_test_aug.values,\n","    'Predicted Yield Strength (MPa)': aug_pred,\n","    'Error (MPa)': errors,\n","    'Absolute Error (MPa)': np.abs(errors)\n","})\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(8,7))\n","plt.scatter(residuals['Actual Yield Strength (MPa)'], residuals['Error (MPa)'], alpha=0.65)\n","plt.axhline(0, linestyle='--')\n","plt.xlabel('Actual Yield Strength (MPa)')\n","plt.ylabel('Prediction Error (MPa)')\n","plt.title('Temperature-Augmented Random Forest: Prediction Errors')\n","plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n","\n","bins=[0,400,600,800,1000,1300,1600,2000,np.inf]\n","labels=['<400','400–600','600–800','800–1000','1000–1300','1300–1600','1600–2000','2000+']\n","residuals['Strength Range']=pd.cut(residuals['Actual Yield Strength (MPa)'], bins=bins, labels=labels)\n","\n","range_summary = residuals.groupby('Strength Range', observed=False).apply(\n","    lambda g: pd.Series({'n':len(g), 'MAE (MPa)':mean_absolute_error(g['Actual Yield Strength (MPa)'],g['Predicted Yield Strength (MPa)']), 'RMSE (MPa)':np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(g['Actual Yield Strength (MPa)'],g['Predicted Yield Strength (MPa)'])), 'Mean Error (MPa)':g['Error (MPa)'].mean()}), include_groups=False\n",")\n","display(range_summary.round(2))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 14. Feature Importance"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["rf_final = final_aug_pipeline.named_steps['random_forest']\n","feature_names = X_aug_raw.columns.tolist()\n","feature_importance = pd.DataFrame({\n","    'Feature': feature_names,\n","    'Importance': rf_final.feature_importances_\n","}).sort_values('Importance', ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\n","\n","display(feature_importance.head(15))\n","\n","top = feature_importance.head(15).sort_values('Importance')\n","plt.figure(figsize=(9,7))\n","plt.barh(top['Feature'], top['Importance'])\n","plt.xlabel('Random Forest Feature Importance')\n","plt.title('Top 15 Features for Yield Strength Prediction')\n","plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 15. Permutation Importance on the Holdout"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["perm = permutation_importance(\n","    final_aug_pipeline, X_test_aug, y_test_aug,\n","    scoring='neg_mean_absolute_error', n_repeats=10,\n","    random_state=RANDOM_STATE, n_jobs=-1\n",")\n","perm_df = pd.DataFrame({\n","    'Feature': X_test_aug.columns,\n","    'Permutation Importance': perm.importances_mean,\n","    'Std': perm.importances_std\n","}).sort_values('Permutation Importance', ascending=False)\n","display(perm_df.head(15))"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 16. Final Interpretation\n","\n","The completed analysis found that chemistry and heat-treatment state provide most of the predictive signal. The temperature-augmented model gives a modest improvement over the core model on the same holdout. The main limitations are sparse observations at very high strength levels and the fact that binary processing flags cannot fully encode detailed thermal histories, cooling rates, phase transformations, or microstructural state.\n","\n","Feature importance indicates predictive association, not metallurgical causation. The high-strength error bins should also be treated as diagnostic because some contain very few test observations."]}],"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.x"}},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":5}